 "remarks": "A rare opportunity in coveted Back Country Greenwich! Offered for the first time in 70 years, this cherished family property presents an exceptional opportunity to reimagine, expand, or create something entirely new on 2.3 acres of beautiful, level land. Set amid tree-lined grounds, the property offers a peaceful setting and a remarkable canvas for its next chapter. The original residence boasts over 3,000 square feet of living space, while the grounds reveal charming handmade treasures that speak to the property's unique history, including a treehouse, barn and detached garage. An existing in-ground pool offers the footprint for a fresh vision. Ideally located near premier country clubs and golf courses, the Audubon Center, prestigious private schools, the Merritt Parkway, I-684 and Westchester County Airport the New York border and the charming town of Armonk. A truly special offering in one of Greenwich's most sought-after settings, with endless possibilities for the discerning buyer, builder or investor. Property to be sold AS IS as part of an estate sale, subject to probate.",
